    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>I have a question about the df in DIF analysis. I ran a sequential DIF analysis, using a graded response model with 3 response option per item.<div>The output of the DIF test gives a X2 with 1 df (see below).</div><div>As 2 models are compared with 3 parameters difference (a, d1, d2) I would expect df=3.</div><div>Can someone explain why df=1 in this case?</div><div><br></div><div>Berend Terluin</div><div><div><br></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">&gt;\r\nmod.freegroup &lt;- multipleGroup(data, 1, group=group, <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">+                      \r\ninvariance = c(&#39;intercepts&#39;,&#39;slopes&#39;, &#39;free_means&#39;, &#39;free_varcov&#39;))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">&gt;\r\nDIF(mod.freegroup, c(&#39;a1&#39;, &#39;d&#39;), seq_stat = .01, scheme = &#39;drop_sequential&#39;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Checking for\r\nDIF in 6 more items<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Checking for\r\nDIF in 4 more items<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Computing\r\nfinal DIF estimates...<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">$DSQ19<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">      \r\nAIC     AICc   \r\nSABIC      BIC   \r\nlogLik     X2  df     p<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">1 49443.78\r\n49446.06 49567.26 49722.94 -24672.89    NaN NaN   NaN<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">2 49434.51\r\n49436.88 49560.51 49719.37 -24667.26 11.266   1 8e-04<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div></div></div>"
    ]
